  "independent_visible_observations": {
    "original": [
      "An open upright circular rim reads as a wide cyan band, a finer aqua outer hoop and evenly spaced small blue rectangular markers, with two dark blue angular boulders supporting its bottom sides.",
      "The central opening is visibly empty. Band and hoop surfaces have large planar facets. The cyan band has a pale upper area and darker lower/side areas; the rocks retain strongly dark triangular faces.",
      "The outer markers read as separate simple blocks; their blue faces have only small edge transitions. There is little warm material in the original."
    ],
    "target": [
      "The open ring identity, cyan/aqua center band, bright blue decorative blocks and paired dark rock supports remain recognizable.",
      "Warm golden trim, raised rounded gold marker housings and gold rock bracing add a distinct constructed frame around the blue elements. The support stones read as dark slate facets with broader lighter planes than the original.",
      "The cyan band appears fuller, with rounded edge transitions and broad soft white/cyan flowing highlights. The gold trim has bright upper bevels and warm shaded side planes. The blue insets have a central face plus faceted bevel faces.",
      "This target is an aesthetic reference only. Its pixels do not establish a future camera, world size, registration, envelope, contact lock or required marker count."
    ],
    "global_style": [
      "The reference plant uses clear broad leaf planes, saturated but separated green light/dark values and warm yellow edge highlights, with softened transitions around an orange/gold pot rim.",
      "Its pot has substantial visible edge thickness, rounded/beveled corners, warm amber side shading and bright upper edging. Forms remain simple and readable, while depth comes from large face relationships and contained highlights.",
      "For comparison with the portal target, both show purposeful warm edge treatment and broad readable facets; the target cyan band contains more continuous flowing highlights than the leaf planes. These observations are independent style comparisons, not a proposed construction recipe or approval."
    ]
  },
